WEBVTT

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:07.600
Satellite punk, do you know how to duel?

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.010
You'll find out soon enough.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.470
You're just gonna quickly 
fail and embarrass yourself.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.440
If you want to quit, now's the time.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.300
What can you do with that lame deck?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.110
Himuro, finish him off fast.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.540
Bro, will you be okay?

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.510
Just watch.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.270
You…

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.440
Who are you?

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:46.980
You're going to learn your place.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.610
Duel!

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:23.390
No matter how far apart we 
are, we can't be stopped

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:28.380
That's deeply engraved into us

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:36.880
So don't be afraid of getting hurt

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.890
Break through even further

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:48.400
While carrying you beliefs in your heart

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:55.550
There's always only one truth

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:59.440
So feel the voice of your heart

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.230
With your unwavering emotions

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:10.330
Seize the signs of tomorrow

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:45.610
Feelings Toward the Cards!  
Crystal Skull vs Giant Ushi Oni

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.450
My turn!  I draw!

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.880
From my hand, I summon Jirai Gumo!

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.180
It appeared!

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.310
All right!  He already summoned 
it on the first turn.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:07.290
Jirai Gumo is Level 4, but it has 2200 
attack points!  Himuro, give him the jitters!

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.930
I set two cards.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.640
I end my turn.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:21.900
Grandpa.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.830
A duel breathes life into cards.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.400
It's the role of the duelist 
to give them that life.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.930
If the cards felt pain 
when that were stepped on,

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.520
then it is the role of the duelist 
to win and give them happiness.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.930
Understood.  Please continue 
to keep an eye on him.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:05.330
The man from Satellite has started 
dueling at the detention center.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:17.600
King, I'm taking you to a room 
that you have never seen before.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:29.550
I'll give you a glimpse of the true nature 
of the Public Maintenance Department.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:14.420
Please calm yourself and look forward.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.650
Have you noticed it?

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:33.440
King, the mark you have on your arm 
symbolizes the wing of the Crimson Dragon.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.960
Crimson Dragon…

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.790
Yes.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:43.760
The Crimson Dragon you saw 
at Duel Stadium, King.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.330
It's my turn.

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:59.090
I had that card in my hand last time.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:05.640
Don't do it!  If you summon that, 
you'll take 1000 points of damage!

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:08.990
I summon Crystal Skull in defense position!

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.640
See, I told you so.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:23.820
You're messing around.  Go 
ahead and self-destruct.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.640
Self-destruct?  Why would I do that?

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:31.230
From my hand, I activate the Quick-Play 
Spell Curse Reflection Doll!

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.150
That card is…

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.330
What?

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:58.800
What's going on?  Himuro 
lost 1000 life points!

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:04.330
And that Satellite punk took zero damage, even 
though he was the one who summoned Crystal Skull.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:07.360
What did you do?  What was that card?

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.200
Curse Reflection Doll.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.400
Due to its effect, the 
damage I take becomes zero,

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.890
and you take damage equal 
to what I would have taken.

00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:21.140
He dealt Crystal Skull's damage to Himuro.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:25.330
You used the curse of Crystal 
Skull to your advantage.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.690
The card answered me.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:35.250
Though derided as useless, Crystal Skull 
gains great power due to the power of its friends.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.920
Friends?

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.340
The cards you gathered are its friends.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:44.240
Bro, you're incredible.

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:50.100
Himuro, that was just luck.  There's no 
way you can lose to a Satellite punk!

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.330
You're wrong.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.410
It wasn't luck.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:55.840
He knows how to duel.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.250
It's getting me excited.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.350
For the first time in awhile, 
I can battle seriously.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.660
I end my turn.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:07.660
This is the first time I've 
seen Himuro look like that.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:10.050
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:16.300
I release Jirai Gumo to summon Ushi Oni!

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.230
Why?  Jirai Gumo has higher attack points.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:24.940
Don't underestimate Himuro!

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.850
The real show is about to start!

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:31.380
I release Ushi Oni to Special 
Summon Giant Ushi Oni!

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.530
Giant Ushi Oni, attack Crystal Skull!

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.080
Himuro is attacking!

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.460
Do it!

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.770
Specter's Bite!

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.120
Giant Ushi Oni's monster effect!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:01.050
When this card destroys one of your monsters 
in battle, it is allowed to attack again!

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:04.320
Attack him directly!

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.510
Bro!

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:11.550
He did it.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.850
He's all talk.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.240
I end my turn.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.050
Now summon a monster!

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:41.460
Neo Domino City's Public Maintenance 
Department is just our current incarnation.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:47.950
We have inherited the power of the people 
of the stars who brings peace to the world.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:52.340
That name is Iliaster.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:54.590
Iliaster?

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:59.190
The word means “the first 
matter of all things.”

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:05.670
Government, economy, military, 
everything that controls the world

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:10.770
is run by the people who 
swear allegiance to Iliaster.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:19.010
I, Rex Godwin, is the 360th star guardian.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.250
From my hand…

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:25.500
I summon Ashoka Pillar in defense position!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.500
There's another one.  A useless stick 
that only has high defense points.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.900
Hurry up and destroy this one too!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.190
Be quiet.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:42.650
Let me see how much you can 
squeeze out of that deck.

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:46.700
From my hand, I activate 
the Equip Spell Stonehenge.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.100
With Stonehenge, I can 
Special Summon a monster

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.290
with zero attack points from the 
graveyard and equip this on to it.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.230
I Special Summon Crystal 
Skull in defense position.

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:07.640
Himuro, you're overestimating him.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:12.860
Bring out Crystal Skull?  Is 
there no limit to his insanity?

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.080
No, you're wrong.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:20.000
After Giant Ushi Oni destroys 
a monster, it can battle again.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.460
If he doesn't have two monsters on his 
field, his life points will instantly become zero.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.570
So those two monsters are 
just for blocking purposes.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:33.610
I see.  He chose a way to survive Himuro's 
attack, even if that meant taking damage.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:37.080
But he made a mistake.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.330
What do you mean?

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:42.810
When Ashoka Pillar is destroyed, 
he takes 2000 points of damage.

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:44.640
That's right, bro.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.840
If Giant Ushi Oni attacks you, it's over.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:50.100
Do you really believe that?

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:55.310
I set one card and end my turn.

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:59.400
Like I thought, he placed a trap.  However…

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.190
That's what I'm aiming for.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.430
Iliaster.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:13.680
It originated 3,000 years ago in the 
Andes Mountains of South America.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:19.350
King, let me lead you to 
the pre-Inca civilization.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:34.090
In the past, the people of the stars built

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:37.090
the 
giant stone civilization known as the temple of heaven.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:41.210
They revered the dragon star, which was said 
to govern all of creation, as their god.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:47.620
All the wisdom held by the stars was handed 
down to the ruler, the star dragon king.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:52.350
Through the star dragon king, the 
people were led by the stars,

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:55.350
and they built a unique 
society and civilization.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:02.870
However, as it happens quite often, 
evil wars threatened the peace.

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:08.940
When that happened, the star dragon king 
prayed to the dragon star for salvation.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:13.010
And the dragon star answered.

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:16.310
The Crimson Dragon, which 
is the incarnation of god,

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:20.000
came down and sealed the incarnation 
of evil into the ground.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.680
Into the ground?

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:24.630
Yes.  Right here.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:30.010
The Nazca Lines?

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:35.130
My turn.  I draw!

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:41.000
I'll see the identity of your set card.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:42.190
Battle!

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:44.950
Stay away!

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:50.060
Giant Ushi Oni, attack Ashoka 
Pillar!  Specter's Bite!

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.760
I activate the Continuous Trap Totem Pole!

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.900
Incredible!

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.420
What?

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:10.320
Totem Pole negates your monsters' 
attacks up to three times.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:14.770
That's pretty good.  I didn't 
know it had that effect.

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:18.940
You fell into my trap, Satellite punk.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:24.000
I activate the Continous 
Trap Spiderweb Castle!

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:30.120
Spiderweb Castle can activate when 
the opponent activates a trap.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:35.580
With this card, when your monster attacks, 
that monster's attack points are halved.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:40.450
Furthermore, if I send this card to the 
graveyard, I can attack you directly.

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:43.760
There's no way you can win, Satellite punk!

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:47.160
Will you be okay, bro?  
Did you hear what he said?

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:50.720
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.870
Now come at me.  My field is perfect.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:15:00.870
With Trap Hole, if you summon a monster with 
1000 or more attack points, it will be destroyed.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:08.390
If you try to attack, Mirror Force will 
destroy all your monsters in attack position.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:11.420
This duel has me fired up.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:15.190
I've forgotten how this felt.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:18.410
It reminds me of that time...

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:25.690
The exciting world of professional 
dueling.  And my final opponent…

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:39.920
You said you were good enough to face 
the King, but this was all you could do?

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.670
This was the worst duel ever.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:47.500
After that, I kept falling.

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:51.880
I quit being a professional.  
However, I couldn't abandon dueling.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:56.300
I competed underground against hooligans 
and barely pulled off victories.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:16:00.500
I clung on to victories among the garbage.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:04.820
I was completely absorbed in illegal 
duels until I finally ended up here.

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:06.950
What a pathetic story.

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:12.600
I like you since you were 
able to get me this excited.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:15.400
I can't lose this duel!

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:17.780
It's my turn.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:22.800
I believe in you.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:28.390
Let's show grandpa your victory.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:32.440
If I can just get one more monster…  Come!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.340
He smiled.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:47.290
I activate the spell card Piri Reis Map!

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:49.690
Who cares.  That's just a map.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:53.560
You shouldn't underestimate it!  Piri 
Reis Map is from the Middle Ages…

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.090
There he goes again.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:56.340
We've had enough of your stories!

00:16:56.470 --> 00:17:02.850
Piri Reis Map allows me to add one monster 
with 0 attack points in my deck to my hand.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:09.710
I summon the card that was added 
to my hand.  Cabrera Stone!

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:19.960
What's that rock?

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:22.040
It's Cabrera Stone!

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.990
It's incredible.  Humans and dinosaurs…

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.010
Enough of your talk!

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:30.240
But what a spectacle!

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:33.990
Crystal Skull and Cabrera 
Stone and Ashoka Pillar!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:39.460
I'm getting goosebumps!  You 
can't see this in any museum!

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.170
What's the meaning of this?

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:44.870
Due to Piri Reis Map's effect, 
if you summon the card

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:48.510
you added to your hand, your 
life points are halved.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:54.090
Now you only have 200 life points.  
Why did you choose that card?

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.840
To win.

00:17:57.490 --> 00:18:02.490
When Crystal Skull, Ashoka Pillar 
and Cabrera Stone are on my field,

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:04.690
there's a card that I can activate.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.040
That's…

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:10.350
I activate the spell card Triangle O!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.590
What?  It's even coming on to my field?

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.260
What?

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:34.960
They'll all be destroyed!

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:39.550
Awesome!  So this is the power of Triangle O!

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:43.860
Triangle O destroys all cards on the field.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:54.010
Then the damage I would have taken due to the 
destroyed cards' effects will be dealt to you.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:10.300
Himuro!  Are you okay?

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.530
Bro, you're awesome!

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:16.830
You won by reflecting back 
3000 points of damage

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:20.630
that you were going to take.  I 
didn't think that was possible.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.830
I just fulfilled the wishes of the cards.

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:26.590
Bro…

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:34.300
He defeated Himuro without 
even battling once.

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:36.880
That punk!  How dare he do this to Himuro!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.170
Wait!

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:39.760
Himuro…

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:45.320
You won without even attacking once.  
You were chosen by the cards.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.690
That was a good strategy.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.440
I'm amazed.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:55.540
I didn't know a duel like this was possible.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.260
What's your name?

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:02.570
Yusei.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.100
Grandpa, I'm sorry that 
I stepped on your cards.

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:11.370
It's fine.  More importantly, look at this.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:15.180
Doesn't it look like 
Crystal Skull is smiling?

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.330
Bro, you're really incredible!

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.070
It would be a waste if you're stuck here.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:24.750
I want to send you to the world of the pros.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.600
Will you duel me again?

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.390
Anytime.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:36.630
Number 88!

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:41.420
The chief wants a word 
with you.  Come with us.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:49.640
The evil was sealed into the ground,

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:54.240
but like rain water seeping 
underground over time,

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:58.600
it has seeped all over the world.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:02.110
Look at the current world.

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:07.660
War, poverty, incurable 
illnesses, economic chaos.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:11.640
There is no peace from the era 
of the people of the stars.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:15.760
The only utopia is Neo Domino City.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.460
You must understand by now.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:22.940
In the near future, the evil god 
sealed in Nazca will resurrect.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:26.130
It will feed on the evil in people's hearts.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.190
What?

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:30.890
We are preparing for the day 
when the evil god resurrects

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:34.840
and will summon the Crimson Dragon 
that will protect the people.

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:39.060
We are searching for Signers that 
have the mark of the dragon.

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:48.280
With this mark, that means I'm one of them.

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:09.630
What can we grasp?  What can we do?

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:15.020
We'll step forward and find out

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:20.950
My unstoppable emotions, the 
beating of my passionate heart

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:26.190
I heard the voice of truth

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:29.350
After I was hurt, I learned

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:34.940
Of a place where I can become stronger

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:42.100
I stack my dreams in my palm

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:47.500
And I'll someday pass them to you

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:53.440
Seeking for the signal 
to start, my soul roars

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:58.780
I will overcome my suffocating 
and mediocre life

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:04.870
I'll dash and acquire all the bright futures

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:14.290
Carrying the bonds I believe 
in, I run towards tomorrow
